# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials — never commit any provider key material.
# Belt (specific): the current Google service-account file at repo root.
voicemodeleval-*.json
# Braces (broad): any Google-style service-account or credential JSON, anywhere.
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*credentials*.json
gcloud-*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
# Standalone secret files: .pem, .key, .p12, .pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# Common secret directories
.secrets/
secrets/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# uv — uv.lock IS committed on purpose. It pins the measuring instrument
# (jiwer, faster-whisper/CTranslate2, TTSDS2), so the +4wk drift re-run can
# attribute a change to the provider rather than to our own toolchain.

# Build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.whl

# Run artifacts (generated audio + logs — regenerable, not versioned)
runs/
judgments/
decisions/

# analysis/*.json outputs are pure functions of runs/ — regenerable,
# not versioned by default. BUT: (a) `analysis/verification/*.md` holds
# human-written Phase 2c verdict artefacts, and (b) the specific
# analyzer outputs that back published claims in the docs are
# committed as evidence (auditability > repo size). Uses `analysis/*`
# (not `analysis/`) so the un-ignore lines below work.
analysis/*
!analysis/verification/
!analysis/campaign-20260809T204608Z/
!analysis/campaign-20260809T204608Z/*.json
!analysis/latency-20260809T214106Z/
!analysis/latency-20260809T214106Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260811T183028Z/
!analysis/latency-20260811T183028Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260811T183202Z/
!analysis/latency-20260811T183202Z/latency.json
# S1b (2026-08-09 T22:23 rerun same day) — cited in the 6-session
# F-11 table alongside S1a.
!analysis/latency-20260809T222356Z/
!analysis/latency-20260809T222356Z/latency.json
# S3 sessions (2026-08-12) with concurrent Cloudflare ping baseline
# — the "S3 doubled" observation that F-11 hangs the "absolute
# values are not stable" claim on.
!analysis/latency-20260812T191143Z/
!analysis/latency-20260812T191143Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260812T191323Z/
!analysis/latency-20260812T191323Z/latency.json
# S4 + S5 sessions (2026-09-01, Phase 2 Follow-up 3) — added by
# the experiment pack. Two ElevenLabs runs (S4 T18:57, S5 T19:10)
# and two OpenAI runs (S4 T19:07, S5 T20:10 — the T19:10 attempt
# collided with the ElevenLabs run-dir and was rerun at T20:10).
!analysis/latency-20260901T185715Z/
!analysis/latency-20260901T185715Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260901T190715Z/
!analysis/latency-20260901T190715Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260901T191000Z/
!analysis/latency-20260901T191000Z/latency.json
!analysis/latency-20260901T201051Z/
!analysis/latency-20260901T201051Z/latency.json
!analysis/variance-20260809T205319Z/
!analysis/variance-20260809T205319Z/*.json
# Ping-baseline log for F-11's S3 latency session — small text file,
# committed as the network-baseline receipt (RTT p50/p90/max, error
# count) so F-11's "ping doesn't move; latency does" claim is
# reproducible without needing the audio runs/.
!analysis/ping-baseline-*.jsonl

# R3 primary campaign (2026-08-31) — same "commit analyzer JSONs, not audio"
# pattern as the R2 campaign above. Backs the R2-vs-R3 replication story
# in EXPERIMENTS_2026-09-01.md and analysis/round3-vs-round2-comparison.md.
!analysis/campaign-20260831T175358Z/
!analysis/campaign-20260831T175358Z/*.json

# T6 campaign — Speechify voice-swap test (20 items × 2 use cases with
# alt voice edmund_32). Load-bearing for F-7's "voice-choice ≥3σ
# survives same-gender matching on Speechify narration" observation.
!analysis/campaign-20260811T180824Z/
!analysis/campaign-20260811T180824Z/*.json

# Round 2 vs Round 3 comparison memo — text file, small, cites the
# committed R2 + R3 analyzer JSONs.
!analysis/round3-vs-round2-comparison.md

# Experiment pack — 2026-09-01 (F-6 deep dive: A/B/C/D/E + follow-ups).
# JSONs (drift, inputs, item1 result), text logs, and API-call logs are
# committed as evidence. WAVs (~200MB) stay ignored — regenerable.
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/*.json
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/*.md
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/inputs/
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/inputs/*.json
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/logs/
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/logs/*.jsonl
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/logs/*.log
# Explicitly exclude the audio subdir — regenerable, ~200MB
analysis/experiments-2026-09-01/audio/

# Synthetic run-store built from experiments-2026-09-01/E audio, for the
# T6-style alt-voice quality/WER analysis. Analyzer output JSONs
# committed; the audio (~130MB copy of E audio) stays ignored.
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01-E/
!analysis/experiments-2026-09-01-E/*.json

# Content-hash cache for synthesis (Phase D.2) — regenerable, safe to nuke
.cache/

# Deviations from prereg — versioned, kept
!DEVIATIONS.md

# Streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Word lock files (left behind by open .docx in documentation/)
~$*

# Local scratch notes under documentation/ — the authoritative record
# lives in configs/ and corpus/, so raw notes are redundant.
documentation/*.txt

# Editors / IDE / Claude Code session state
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp

# Vercel
voting/node_modules/
voting/.vercel/
voting/dist/

# Phase F rating pipeline — only the source page + tests belong in git.
# Per-rater manifests, normalized audio, anchor recordings, and judgment
# CSVs are all ephemeral / personal / regenerable via `veval rate ...`.
rating/audio/
rating/anchor/
rating/manifest.json
# Generated derivative of the corpus (regeneratable via `uv run python
# scripts/anchor_script.py`). Committing would just be noise churn on
# every corpus tweak.
rating/anchor_script.md
# Judgment CSVs — private per-rater data (may include timing / preference
# signal that a rater hasn't consented to publish).
judgments-*.csv
documentation/judgement_tests/
documentation/judgment_tests/

# Phase G rendered outputs — derivative of `analysis/score.json`,
# regenerable via `veval report`. The score JSON (in analysis/) IS
# committed as the receipt; the rendered memos + charts are not.
site/

# Round-30 review defect register — a personal working checklist (40 items,
# what's wrong / plain-language / the fix), not part of the published research
# output. Ticked-off progress lives in browser localStorage, so the file itself
# is a static snapshot; the live copy with cross-device sync is the claude.ai
# artifact. Regenerable, personal, and would only churn the diff — not versioned.
DEFECT_REGISTER_R30.html
